  "en": {
    "__title": "Imberion — Street Signal",
    "familia_label": "Signal · sense",
    "hero_eyebrow": "Street Signal · Signal family",
    "hero_h1": "What to buy, import and display, based on what people wear on the street.",
    "hero_lead": "Street Signal measures what people walking down the street are wearing: garment, style and, when it can be read, brand, along with the apparent profile of the person wearing it. Footage is captured at different points, hours, days and weather. Data comes out anonymized: the system records the apparent profile and what the person is wearing, with no personal or biometric data. It applies to fashion and apparel.",
    "que_hace_h2": "What it solves in the assortment",
    "que_hace_p": "The buying team decides with what people wear on the street in each area, in addition to what has already sold in store.",
    "que_hace_items": [
      "Share of each brand on the street, by area and by profile",
      "Wardrobe by customer profile: which garments and styles they wear",
      "Garments and styles worth buying and importing, located by area",
      "What goes in the shop window, based on who walks past the store",
      "Profile-led selling: what to offer each type of customer"
    ],
    "valor_h2": "From the street to the assortment",
    "valor_p": "With brand share on the street by area, buying sees which brand and which garment people in that area wear, and adjusts what it buys and imports for the stores located there. With the wardrobe by profile, the shop window and profile-led selling start from what that profile already wears.",
